## Section C: Design Scenario (22 marks)

A company will build **100,000 soil-moisture sensors**. Each unit:

- Wakes every 15 minutes, reads an ADC, and transmits 20 bytes over a low-power radio
- Must last **3 years** on a **1,000 mAh** battery
- Operates outdoors from −10 °C to 60 °C with no maintenance
- Has a target of **$1.50** or less for the MCU

**(a)** (6) Choose between an MCU-based and an MPU-based design. Justify your choice against **all four** constraints: power, size, cost and reliability.

**(b)** (6) Assume you must derate the battery by 20%. Calculate the **maximum average current** the device may draw. Show your working and state your answer in µA.

**(c)** (5) Propose a software stack for this product. Name one component for each layer (drivers, middleware, application) and state where a HAL fits and one trade-off of using it here.

**(d)** (5) Name **two** reliability measures you would include in the firmware and **one** toolchain setting that would reduce flash use. Explain each briefly.

